    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4e9936a0c8c4858de169ad0d9050cd952b0014030b871080d89321df0a5ee334",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At a positive integer k, the q-zeta specialization reduces after rescaling to a Lambert-series limit for zeta(k). For even k>=4, that same Lambert sum is the nonconstant Fourier part of the weight-k Eisenstein series, so modular inversion converts the q-to-1 asymptotic into its Bernoulli constant term.",
